; DOMAIN: kudla-program [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: The Kudla program predicts that generating series of special (arithmetic) cycles on orthogonal and unitary Shimura varieties are modular: the formal generating function sum_T Z(T) q^T, whose coefficients are special cycle classes (in Chow groups or arithmetic Chow groups), is a Siegel modular form of appropriate weight and genus. This generalizes Gross-Kohnen-Zagier (143, weight-3/2 case on modular curves) to higher-dimensional Shimura varieties, and connects arithmetic intersection numbers of these cycles to derivatives of Siegel-Eisenstein series and Rankin-Selberg L-functions, unifying the Yuan-Zhang-Zhang (141) height and Waldspurger (142) period formulas within a single arithmetic-theta framework. Bridge: genesis_gross_kohnen (weight-3/2 modular generating series, the codimension-1 antecedent) + genesis_waldspurger (theta/period companion) + genesis_yuan_zhang_zhang (arithmetic-height side) + genesis_heegner_points (special cycles of dimension 0).
(= (kudla-generating-series $V $n) (siegel-modular-form (genus $n) (coefficients (lambda ($T) (special-cycle-class $V $T)))))
(= (kudla-generalizes-gkz $V) (implies (codimension $V 1) (gkz-generating-series $V)))
(= (arithmetic-intersection-l-derivative $V $T) (equal (arithmetic-degree (special-cycle $V $T)) (l-derivative (siegel-eisenstein $T) (central-point))))